THOUGHT: NullAway complains that the constructor doesn’t guarantee non-null initialization of button1 and button2. They are only set via protected setters, so subclasses might forget to call them. The simplest fix is to mark these fields as @Nullable and adjust their getters accordingly, but that would ripple to callers. A better fix is to ensure they are initialized in the base constructor with safe default ImageComponent instances, so they’re never null even if subclasses don’t override them. I’ll inspect ImageComponent to construct minimal dummy components, then update the constructor to create default buttons and ensure sliderComponent is non-null before it’s used in the onChange lambda.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && \
nl -ba src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/gui/ImageComponent.java | sed -n '1,200p' && \
sed -i '25,40s/.*/  protected Slider(
      final double x,
      final double y,
      final double width,
      final double height,
      final float minValue,
      final float maxValue,
      final float stepSize) {
    super(x, y, width, height);
    this.changeConsumer = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();
    this.minValue = minValue;
    this.maxValue = maxValue;
    this.stepSize = stepSize;
    // initialize default components to satisfy @NonNull guarantees
    this.button1 = new ImageComponent(x, y, 0, 0);
    this.button2 = new ImageComponent(x, y, 0, 0);
    this.sliderComponent = new ImageComponent(x, y, 0, 0);
    this.onChange(e -> this.sliderComponent.setLocation(this.getRelativeSliderPosition()));
  }/' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/gui/Slider.java && \
./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && \
grep -E "NullAway|error: \[NullAway\]" -n new_build_output.log | tail -n 20 && \
grep -E "errors\]" new_build_output.log | tail -n 5
```

